{"term":"linger","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c42f1f7d75f79125c1","definition":"To stay or remain in a place or situation, especially as if unwilling to depart or not easily able to do so.","example":"Still more foole I ſhall appeare / By the time I linger here","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abide","loiter","tarry","abide","eld","linger","retard","stay","tarry","wait"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["lingerer","lingering","lingerly","linger on","linger out","lingersome","outlinger","overlinger"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linger#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7daa042d55d53c80d2","definition":"To remain alive or existent although still proceeding toward death or extinction; to die gradually.","example":"He lingered through the day, and died that evening as the sun went down.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["lingerer","lingering","lingerly","linger on","linger out","lingersome","outlinger","overlinger"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linger#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:07406155057a83a212","definition":"To consider or contemplate for a period of time; to engage in analytic thinking or discussion.","example":"Trump doesn't linger on the poll.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"idiomatic, often","register":"idiomatic, intransitive, often","wordFamily":["lingerer","lingering","lingerly","linger on","linger out","lingersome","outlinger","overlinger"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/linger#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3822c2b0b4b0ff8dfb","definition